# Drivers holds planning inputs and calculates nothing; this file only carries
# feeders. TM1 ignores every feeder in a rules file without SKIPCHECK.
# SKIPCHECK also restores sparse consolidation, which leaves Drivers' figures
# unchanged, because every Drivers cell is stored.
# The New South Wales threshold credit in PnL reads the threshold from here,
# and the Workforce payroll tax feeder does not reach it when the designated
# group employer's own payroll tax is nil. A threshold therefore feeds the
# credit's FY consolidation, which feeds each of its months.
SKIPCHECK;

FEEDERS;
['Full Year', 'Payroll Tax Threshold'] => DB('PnL', !Year, !Version, 'FY', 'CivilCo', 'Corporate', 'Payroll Tax', 'Amount');
